<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <AnalysisLevel>latest</AnalysisLevel>
    <Version>3.0.0-alpha.1</Version>
    <Company>SilexGIS</Company>
    <Product>SilexGIS</Product>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>AGPL-3.0-or-later</PackageLicenseExpression>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Five advisories against SixLabors.ImageSharp, accepted here by name rather than fixed.

    NPOI 2.7.6 brings ImageSharp 2.x in transitively. The advisories cover every ImageSharp release
    up to 4.1.1 and are first patched in 4.1.2, whose API NPOI 2.7.6 cannot use — so there is no
    version to move to. NPOI's own answer is 2.8.1, which drops ImageSharp for SkiaSharp, but 2.8.x
    requires accepting the Open Source Maintenance Fee EULA: a paid-licence commitment, which is a
    decision for the project's owner and not a way to fix a build.

    What is being accepted. All five are in image decoding and processing — ICC colour-profile
    parsing and histogram equalisation. Nothing in this solution decodes an image through NPOI: it
    is used by two classes, one writing spreadsheet cells and one extracting text from legacy
    Office files, and neither mentions a picture, an image or a drawing. The vulnerable code ships
    in the package and is not reached from here.

    Here rather than in the project that references NPOI, because an audit suppression does not
    cross a project reference: the API project sees the same transitive package and failed on it
    while Infrastructure was quiet.

    Named advisories and not the NU1902/NU1903 categories, deliberately — the next advisory against
    anything at all is still an error that stops the build, which is the only reason this one was
    noticed. A clean restore had begun failing while warm caches went on succeeding.

    Revisit when the owner has decided about the NPOI licence, or when a 2.7.x release asks for
    ImageSharp 4.1.2.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-gwg2-r3hj-4w44" />
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j3p4-wp97-rph4" />
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j9gm-c75j-xc9q" />
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jjfr-hcj7-qf5w" />
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-wmxv-xphr-5c9g" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
